sequenceDiagram
  actor User as Member / Staff / Admin
  participant API as Cancel adapter (JWT, role, owner)
  participant Key as IdempotencyService
  participant Cancel as CancelOrderService
  participant DB as MongoDB replica set
  participant Worker as OrderExpiryWorker
  User->>API: POST cancel {version, reason} + UUIDv4
  API->>Key: normalized DTO + target + channel
  Key->>DB: transaction snapshot/majority/primary
  alt committed same key
    DB-->>Key: original response (owner checked)
  else new key
    Key->>Cancel: same session
    Cancel->>DB: gates member → inventory → transaction → order
    Cancel->>DB: re-read version/state, payment, reservation ledger
    alt already CANCELLED
      DB-->>Cancel: terminal state + current refund, retain reason
    else HELD and PENDING/CONFIRMED
      Cancel->>DB: ORDER_RELEASE each item, reserved−q
      Cancel->>DB: PENDING transaction→CANCELLED or SETTLED→retain + refund PENDING
      Cancel->>DB: order CANCELLED/RELEASED, event + notification/outbox
    end
    Key->>DB: operation result + commit together
  end
  API-->>User: 200 state + obligation (not paid out)
  Worker->>DB: every5s, overdue HELD batch50, sorted expiry/id
  loop each overdue order
    Worker->>Cancel: expire (SYSTEM), own transaction, fresh clock after gates
    Note over Cancel,DB: same transition, no fake account ID; isolate errors/backoff≤60s
  end
  User->>API: STAFF/ADMIN POST late-receipts + key
  API->>Key: RETAIL_LATE_RECEIPT
  Key->>DB: member → transaction → order gates
  Key->>DB: verify CANCELLED/RELEASED, no succeeded payment, full TRANSFER
  Key->>DB: payment SUCCEEDED + refund PENDING + event/outbox/key commit
  Note over Key,DB: no inventory change, SETTLED, sale invoice or reopen
  API-->>User: paymentId + refundId, transaction remains CANCELLED
